From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:23:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: provide an acpi_has_method() stub without CONFIG_ACPI

btintel_set_dsm_reset_method() calls acpi_has_method() after an early
return when ACPI_HANDLE() is NULL, which it always is without
CONFIG_ACPI.  An optimizing compiler removes the dead call; one that
keeps it (tinycc, or gcc -O0) leaves an undefined reference, since
acpi_has_method() has no stub for the !ACPI case.  Give it one in
acpi_bus.h, which btintel.c includes directly, so that drivers can use
it unconditionally.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 include/acpi/acpi_bus.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/acpi/acpi_bus.h b/include/acpi/acpi_bus.h
index a10a591c1..2cba28b8c 100644
--- a/include/acpi/acpi_bus.h
+++ b/include/acpi/acpi_bus.h
@@ -45,7 +45,14 @@ acpi_status
 acpi_evaluate_ost(acpi_handle handle, u32 source_event, u32 status_code,
 		  struct acpi_buffer *status_buf);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ACPI
 bool acpi_has_method(acpi_handle handle, char *name);
+#else
+static inline bool acpi_has_method(acpi_handle handle, char *name)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+#endif
 acpi_status acpi_execute_simple_method(acpi_handle handle, char *method,
 				       u64 arg);
 acpi_status acpi_evaluate_ej0(acpi_handle handle);
